  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency WASH response to South Sudanese refugees in WN state</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project, a response to the South Sudanese civil war and the flight of refugees to Sudan, expands the provision of WASH services in refugee camps in White Nile state. CAFOD through its national partner SIDO are responsible for WASH services in Alagaya camp, Dabat Bosin camp, Um Sangor camp, Jory host community village and Dabat Bosin host community village. 

The following interventions are planned:
(1) Latrines will be constructed, and hygiene promotion packages provided, for 700 households in the new Alagaya extension site, complementing WASH services that CAFOD is providing through its national partner in the nearby Alagaya camp. Temporary water points will also be supplied using water trucking until the water station is finalized by UNICEF. 
(2) In Um Sangor camp, CAFOD will enhance the recently constructed (in partnership with UNHCR) latrines by providing sandbags for flooding protection, and introducing step ladders to make it easier for the old and disabled to access them.</narrative>
  </description>
